// A magnitude past i64 max is an ERROR, never a silent wrap (DEC-019): the
// accumulator is capped exactly like the seed lexer's accumulate_digit, with
// the lexer's own wording under the str_to_int prefix — i64 min is equally
// out of reach, because the source literal -9223372036854775808 fails the
// same way (the sign is not part of the literal the lexer accumulates).
// EXPECT-RUNTIME-ERROR: str_to_int: integer literal is out of range for i64
fn main() {
    print(str_to_int("9223372036854775808"))
}
